{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Why from Shaddai</b> — most of the commentators interpret:" "<b>Shaddai</b> — in this place [it means] שדד (dealt destruction), and its meaning is: why are times not hidden by Shaddai." "<b>And those who know Him</b> — do not see the days, and the matter is: had times been hidden by Shaddai, I would not complain against Him, for those who know Him do not know what will be; rather, it is He who knows the times in which the wicked act — the wicked, why does He keep silent."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:03:31.870421081Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}